1
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,867
Hi, Guys!

2
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,600
Today, we are here
at Bolagos National High School.

3
00:00:19,733 --> 00:00:21,600
Of course,
I am with my very demure,

4
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:24,667
very mindful,
and very cutesy mother,

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,300
who is very dear to me.
Soafer pretty.

6
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:29,767
Mother, strike a pose there,
Mother.

7
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,133
There you go!

8
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:32,200
And...

9
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,233
Go ahead, Mother.

10
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,767
And for sure, you know why we
are here today.

11
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,033
Of course,

12
00:00:38,167 --> 00:00:41,833
it's the Pillar of Progress
Annual Awards Community Service.

13
00:00:41,967 --> 00:00:44,267
And now, we will honor our
fellow citizen

14
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:49,267
who truly love and serve
our town, Bolagos.

15
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:53,400
And with us are our brave
police officers.

16
00:00:54,267 --> 00:00:55,200
Hi!

17
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:57,833
Yes!

18
00:00:57,967 --> 00:01:01,433
You know, I really admire them
because in events like this,

19
00:01:01,567 --> 00:01:03,367
they protect us,
they take care of us.

20
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:07,167
And of course,
they always respond

21
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:10,133
when there are super dangerous
situations.

22
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,833
It's really dangerous!

23
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:15,233
Ka-Tirada guys...

24
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,633
In three months,

25
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:20,733
the crime rate in the country
has increased

26
00:01:20,867 --> 00:01:22,133
by thirty-five percent.

27
00:01:22,267 --> 00:01:23,567
Where will that lead us?

28
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:32,033
Robbery, holdup, abuse, rape,
and murder are rampant.

29
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:36,567
And according to the data,
addicts are often the culprits.

30
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:37,833
Oh my, it's driving me crazy!

31
00:01:37,967 --> 00:01:41,767
When we watch the news,
all we see is bad news.

32
00:01:41,933 --> 00:01:44,267
So it's good that there
are events like this

33
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,133
that can really restore our
faith in humanity.

34
00:01:47,267 --> 00:01:48,300
Right or wrong?

35
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:52,433
As for me, I do believe that
they do deserve their awards,

36
00:01:52,567 --> 00:01:55,033
that they should be truly
honored.

37
00:01:55,167 --> 00:02:00,433
And of course, I know one
of the awardees today...

38
00:02:00,567 --> 00:02:01,900
What, you want a clue?

39
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:06,933
Brave, efficient, kind,
hardworking,

40
00:02:07,067 --> 00:02:09,200
and of course, handsome.

41
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:12,033
What? Are you excited, right?

42
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,233
May I request all the awardees
to proceed

43
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,733
to the backstage area.

44
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:17,700
This is it!

45
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:19,533
Miguel...

46
00:02:20,133 --> 00:02:21,367
You're embarrassing.

47
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:23,467
The program is about to start.

48
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:25,167
<i> There's just a sudden tip.</i>

49
00:02:26,767 --> 00:02:28,800
Everything is sudden
when it comes to you,

50
00:02:28,933 --> 00:02:30,567
you're so hard to depend on.

51
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,533
You always have an excuse.

52
00:02:32,667 --> 00:02:36,500
Just say that you have no
consideration for other people.

53
00:02:41,167 --> 00:02:43,633
Mother, he's still not here?

54
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:48,833
Who's going to be happy?

55
00:02:48,967 --> 00:02:51,500
The crime rate in the country
is getting worse and worse.

56
00:02:51,633 --> 00:02:52,767
And do you know why?

57
00:02:54,733 --> 00:02:57,300
Because there's something
even scarier

58
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,933
than criminals and syndicates.

59
00:03:05,833 --> 00:03:08,067
The ones in uniform

60
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:11,267
and with badges.

61
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,033
They're the scariest.

62
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,467
They're the most dangerous.

63
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,167
The police,

64
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:32,333
who should be our protectors

65
00:03:32,467 --> 00:03:37,433
but now the criminals and
syndicates are being protected.

66
00:03:37,567 --> 00:03:38,800
This is okay.

67
00:03:38,933 --> 00:03:41,567
Go ahead, Gonzalo,
let them pass.

68
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:43,633
But don't worry, Ka-Tiradas.

69
00:03:45,067 --> 00:03:49,167
We won't stop fighting
for the truth.

70
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,000
Anyone,

71
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,467
anywhere.

72
00:04:14,833 --> 00:04:15,700
What's inside?

73
00:04:17,967 --> 00:04:19,600
We checked it, Sir.

74
00:04:19,733 --> 00:04:21,467
The paper is clean. Good to go.

75
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:23,700
I want to see it.

76
00:04:23,833 --> 00:04:25,567
Mother, just chill.

77
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:29,300
Maybe Father has an urgent
matter to attend to.

78
00:04:29,467 --> 00:04:30,533
Urgent?

79
00:04:31,567 --> 00:04:33,200
Isn't this urgent, too?

80
00:04:33,333 --> 00:04:36,300
My child, do you know that some
of the awardees are here

81
00:04:36,433 --> 00:04:38,733
two hours before their call
time?

82
00:04:38,867 --> 00:04:42,167
They're here because this
is so important to them.

83
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,900
But your father?

84
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:47,067
Nothing. No word from him.

85
00:04:47,767 --> 00:04:49,833
He doesn't even know
how to give updates.

86
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:15,033
Your Father, maybe he's busy
with something else.

87
00:05:15,167 --> 00:05:17,133
That's why he's still not here.

88
00:05:18,033 --> 00:05:19,967
Mother, let's just wait for him.

89
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:22,533
Father will still show up.

90
00:05:23,933 --> 00:05:24,967
No need.

91
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,000
You know,

92
00:05:27,533 --> 00:05:29,700
we're the only ones who are
being affected

93
00:05:29,833 --> 00:05:32,467
because of his irresponsibility.

94
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:36,267
Let him explain to the organizer
when he gets here.

95
00:05:37,767 --> 00:05:39,733
Mother, where are you going?

96
00:05:40,933 --> 00:05:41,933
I'm going home.

97
00:05:42,567 --> 00:05:43,133
What?

98
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:44,667
I'm going home.

99
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:49,233
I have more important things
to do in my life than wait here.

100
00:06:03,367 --> 00:06:04,600
Run, hurry!

101
00:06:12,367 --> 00:06:13,567
Call for backup!

102
00:06:36,233 --> 00:06:38,133
Aren't we starting yet?

103
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:40,033
We're going to cover something
in Amoroso.

104
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:42,167
They say they're still waiting
for someone.

105
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:44,100
Another awardee
who is a police officer.

106
00:06:45,933 --> 00:06:46,733
Troublemaker.

107
00:06:48,467 --> 00:06:50,367
Later, later.

108
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,967
Sir Andrew is busy.
Later, just go back.

109
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,333
You're getting in the way.

110
00:06:56,467 --> 00:06:58,300
Hello, hello.

111
00:06:58,433 --> 00:07:00,667
Boss, sorry. They're stubborn.

112
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,000
Okay, that's okay.

113
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,233
Okay, take a picture of us.

114
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,567
Okay. I'll just take a picture.

115
00:07:07,833 --> 00:07:09,233
Just a group pic.

116
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:11,767
One...

117
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,100
One, two, three...

118
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:15,700
That's it!

119
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:18,733
Grandmother...

120
00:07:19,433 --> 00:07:20,533
Are you okay?

121
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,933
Do you want to take a picture
with me?

122
00:07:23,900 --> 00:07:24,833
Okay, I'll take a picture.

123
00:07:24,967 --> 00:07:25,900
Okay.

124
00:07:26,033 --> 00:07:27,200
Help me.

125
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:29,633
Smile.

126
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:33,867
- Thank you.
- Oh my god...

127
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Andrew, Andrew, look.

128
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,500
That's Bolagos.

129
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:42,800
The chase is still ongoing.

130
00:07:43,333 --> 00:07:45,000
Posted 1 minute ago.

131
00:07:45,133 --> 00:07:46,800
It looks like it's still
ongoing.

132
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,833
Look for the upload.

133
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,100
Full footage if there is one.

134
00:07:50,233 --> 00:07:51,200
Okay, Boss.

135
00:07:51,533 --> 00:07:53,100
-Got it. We'll gather the intel.
-Put that video on the feed.

136
00:07:53,233 --> 00:07:55,333
I'm going live.

137
00:07:55,467 --> 00:07:57,767
<i>Your number cannot be completed
as dialed.</i>

138
00:07:57,900 --> 00:07:59,767
<i>Please check the number
and dial.</i>

139
00:08:09,967 --> 00:08:11,033
Where is the backup?

140
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:12,633
Ramon is still not answering,
Sir.

141
00:08:41,133 --> 00:08:42,967
Who are the police chasing

142
00:08:43,100 --> 00:08:46,000
and what's in the truck
they're carrying?

143
00:08:46,133 --> 00:08:48,500
But the bigger question,
Ka-Tiradas,

144
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:50,433
is why did it come to this?

145
00:08:50,567 --> 00:08:52,633
Did someone break protocol?

146
00:08:52,767 --> 00:08:55,600
You can be rest assured
that if someone is involved,

147
00:08:55,767 --> 00:08:57,567
we'll make sure someone is held
accountable.

148
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,467
Hey!

149
00:09:24,467 --> 00:09:25,533
We can't go far!

150
00:09:25,667 --> 00:09:26,833
The tire blew!

151
00:09:26,967 --> 00:09:29,500
Try to stop,
I'll blow your skull off.

152
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:48,700
Make sure everyone involved
is caught on camera, okay?

153
00:09:52,033 --> 00:09:53,267
Move!

154
00:10:07,300 --> 00:10:08,933
Andrew, where are you going?

155
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,400
Move!

156
00:10:21,900 --> 00:10:23,400
Someone's shooting!

157
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:51,200
Stupid!

158
00:10:52,567 --> 00:10:54,067
Grandmother...

159
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,367
Grandmother, are you okay?

160
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:59,033
Let's get out of here,
Grandmother.

161
00:11:08,300 --> 00:11:12,067
Hey guys, I'm still here
at Bolagos National High School,

162
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:14,367
where the awarding ceremony
was disrupted.

163
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,767
Because of this.

164
00:11:19,367 --> 00:11:20,133
Here. That's it.

165
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:22,533
There's an armed man
in that truck.

166
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:24,667
Come on!

167
00:11:25,167 --> 00:11:26,300
Come on!

168
00:12:32,533 --> 00:12:34,567
There are civilians. Be careful.

169
00:12:43,233 --> 00:12:44,400
Sir, don't!

170
00:12:46,033 --> 00:12:47,700
I'm not with them!

171
00:13:30,033 --> 00:13:31,500
Cruz, cover me!

172
00:13:35,867 --> 00:13:37,233
- Ouch.
- Andrew!

173
00:13:37,367 --> 00:13:39,533
You take care of Grandmother.

174
00:13:39,667 --> 00:13:41,167
Okay. Why? What are you going
to do?

175
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:42,767
I'll cover the shootout.

176
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:44,067
Andrew, it's dangerous!

177
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:45,533
Take care of Grandmother.

178
00:13:59,333 --> 00:14:00,933
Let's finish that cop.

179
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,233
Let's go together.

180
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,367
Who are you?

181
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:33,833
Check it out.

182
00:14:45,267 --> 00:14:46,567
You're so stupid.

183
00:15:56,767 --> 00:15:58,333
Are you looking for me?

184
00:15:58,467 --> 00:16:00,200
Go ahead and shoot.

185
00:16:00,333 --> 00:16:01,800
This kid is dead.

186
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,533
Shoot!

187
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:09,767
What?

188
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:10,967
You can't do it.

189
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:12,233
If I were you,

190
00:16:12,367 --> 00:16:14,133
drop what you're holding.

191
00:16:15,233 --> 00:16:16,367
Drop it!

192
00:16:34,933 --> 00:16:36,400
You're not allowed here!
Get out of here!

193
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,000
Let go of that kid.

194
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,233
I'll take care of you.

195
00:16:43,367 --> 00:16:44,767
I'm not stupid!

196
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:46,300
I don't have a weapon anymore.

197
00:16:46,433 --> 00:16:47,400
Let her go.

198
00:16:47,933 --> 00:16:49,733
I don't care!

199
00:16:49,867 --> 00:16:55,067
If I were you, let me go
so we can keep this kid alive.

200
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,333
What?

201
00:16:57,533 --> 00:16:58,800
Don't be annoying!

202
00:16:59,767 --> 00:17:02,500
Just give up! You can't escape!

203
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,167
What are you saying?

204
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:07,367
I'll kill you.

205
00:17:08,067 --> 00:17:09,533
I'm not afraid of you.

206
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:12,567
My father said...

207
00:17:13,933 --> 00:17:15,500
Never say die!

208
00:17:20,400 --> 00:17:21,000
What?

209
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:22,767
Never say die!

210
00:17:33,967 --> 00:17:34,667
Are you okay?

211
00:17:36,067 --> 00:17:37,467
Of course, Father.

212
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:38,600
You're here.

213
00:17:42,033 --> 00:17:44,433
Then, the caller,
I sent you the text.

214
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,100
Andrew, what happened to you?

215
00:17:49,533 --> 00:17:50,133
Are you okay?

216
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:51,133
Update.

217
00:17:52,033 --> 00:17:53,633
What's in the truck?

218
00:18:02,267 --> 00:18:03,833
Congratulations, Major Delgado.

219
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,600
This looks like a solid hit.

220
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:08,800
Thank you, Chief.

221
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:14,100
Captain Olarve's team will
take custody from here.

222
00:18:14,233 --> 00:18:15,433
Affirmative, Sir.

223
00:18:16,133 --> 00:18:19,567
And we'll handle the inventory
and take it to the lab

224
00:18:20,067 --> 00:18:21,200
for verifications.

225
00:18:22,167 --> 00:18:23,233
Thank you, Captain.

226
00:18:23,367 --> 00:18:25,267
How much is the street value
of that, Cap?

227
00:18:26,067 --> 00:18:29,467
Based on intel,
800 million pesos,

228
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:30,467
rough estimate.

229
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:32,233
800 million?

230
00:18:33,033 --> 00:18:36,467
Sir, you saved an entire city
of addicts.

231
00:18:38,933 --> 00:18:40,167
This is a huge shipment.

232
00:18:40,733 --> 00:18:44,867
But I'm sure there's someone
bigger behind this.

233
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:46,367
For sure.

234
00:18:48,400 --> 00:18:50,933
The drug bust operation here
in the province of Bolagos

235
00:18:51,067 --> 00:18:52,433
is now under control.

236
00:18:53,167 --> 00:18:55,833
Job well done, Bolagos Police.

237
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,067
But the town's tirade is,

238
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,600
was it really just a simple
operation

239
00:19:00,733 --> 00:19:03,467
or is it a drug deal gone wrong?

240
00:19:03,733 --> 00:19:04,400
Cut.

241
00:19:06,167 --> 00:19:07,033
Okay.

242
00:19:07,167 --> 00:19:08,533
Let's go inside.

243
00:19:09,467 --> 00:19:10,533
We'll just change the battery,
Sir.

244
00:19:10,667 --> 00:19:11,533
Okay, thank you.

245
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:18,000
Grandmother...

246
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:19,800
Grandmother,
why are you still here?

247
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:21,867
I thought you had gone home
already.

248
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,033
I haven't said thank you yet.

249
00:19:24,167 --> 00:19:25,767
Oh my, Ka-Saludos!

250
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,267
Too bad the ceremony
didn't push through today

251
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,833
because of what happened.

252
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,033
But I'm still really proud
of my father.

253
00:19:32,167 --> 00:19:34,400
Later, we'll try to interview
him?

254
00:19:34,533 --> 00:19:36,167
If he agrees.

255
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,967
Okay, Ka-Saludo guys!

256
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:39,800
Okay, okay, I'll get back
to you.

257
00:19:39,933 --> 00:19:41,800
See you guys later!

258
00:19:42,067 --> 00:19:42,967
But, Grandmother,

259
00:19:43,767 --> 00:19:45,500
I hope you go home.

260
00:19:45,633 --> 00:19:49,367
And, I promise,
I'll be good at my job,

261
00:19:49,767 --> 00:19:51,133
especially since I know you're
watching.

262
00:19:51,933 --> 00:19:54,333
Thank you very much.

263
00:19:54,467 --> 00:19:55,500
We'll go ahead.

264
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:56,467
Okay.

265
00:19:58,633 --> 00:19:59,767
Take care.

266
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,133
Wow...

267
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:04,300
That's great, he's kind.

268
00:20:04,433 --> 00:20:06,833
You're so sweet, aren't you?

269
00:20:06,967 --> 00:20:09,767
What chapter is that in your
Boss Budol Guide Book?

270
00:20:10,133 --> 00:20:11,933
The good guy angle.

271
00:20:12,067 --> 00:20:13,867
You look familiar.

272
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,800
You're so OA.

273
00:20:15,933 --> 00:20:17,733
Well, that was just one
incident, right?

274
00:20:17,867 --> 00:20:20,500
Okay, show me your data.

275
00:20:21,633 --> 00:20:22,833
Right, right.

276
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,600
That's why.

277
00:20:24,733 --> 00:20:26,167
My basher.

278
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,433
JoeyOnDuty?

279
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:29,000
Am I right?

280
00:20:29,267 --> 00:20:29,933
That's me,

281
00:20:30,667 --> 00:20:31,900
but I'm not a basher.

282
00:20:33,267 --> 00:20:37,667
I'm a legit content creator
making legit content.

283
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:38,967
Wow!

284
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,433
You know, it's a good thing
I caught up with you

285
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,100
because I have a lot of
questions

286
00:20:43,233 --> 00:20:47,900
about your anti-police tirades
and your budol tactics.

287
00:20:48,033 --> 00:20:49,500
That's great.

288
00:20:49,633 --> 00:20:53,733
You're really no different,
right, in person and on video?

289
00:20:53,867 --> 00:21:00,133
Same confidence, same arrogance,
same no substance, right?

290
00:21:00,267 --> 00:21:00,900
Wow...

291
00:21:01,033 --> 00:21:02,267
It's just noise.

292
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:05,067
Wow, look who's talking, someone
who is trying to be deep.

293
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:07,300
But we're just the same.

294
00:21:07,433 --> 00:21:08,967
We're both real talk.

295
00:21:09,133 --> 00:21:11,167
You know the only difference
between us?

296
00:21:12,500 --> 00:21:14,367
You just have more ring light.

297
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:17,933
You're funny.

298
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:20,267
Guys, let's go back to work.

299
00:21:21,667 --> 00:21:23,567
The real journalism.

300
00:21:34,967 --> 00:21:38,100
We don't have a name yet,
but it's not a small syndicate.

301
00:21:38,233 --> 00:21:42,000
We have two in custody thanks
to the brave police officers,

302
00:21:42,167 --> 00:21:47,600
Major Miguel Delgado
and Master Sergeant Steve Cruz.

303
00:21:47,733 --> 00:21:48,500
Major,

304
00:21:50,533 --> 00:21:52,967
how did you know about this kind
of drug transport?

305
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:56,167
I think this is your second time
intercepting

306
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,967
this kind of operation,
isn't it?

307
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:01,200
You're very lucky.

308
00:22:01,333 --> 00:22:04,933
Or maybe you have inside
knowledge

309
00:22:05,233 --> 00:22:06,800
about this kind of shipment.

310
00:22:15,733 --> 00:22:17,533
What do you want to point out
with your question?

311
00:22:17,767 --> 00:22:18,767
Get straight to the point.

312
00:22:19,067 --> 00:22:21,233
It's not that hard to answer
my question

313
00:22:21,733 --> 00:22:23,333
if you're not hiding anything.

314
00:22:23,933 --> 00:22:25,100
I'm not hiding anything,

315
00:22:26,067 --> 00:22:27,633
but with the tone of your voice,

316
00:22:28,900 --> 00:22:30,867
it seems like you want to say
that I'm an accomplice in this.

317
00:22:31,667 --> 00:22:32,633
Are you involved?

318
00:22:34,300 --> 00:22:36,267
Let's save it for the press
conference.

319
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:38,567
Thank you. Let's go, Major.

320
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:49,933
You're really savage.

321
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:53,500
Let's go?

322
00:22:53,633 --> 00:22:54,967
Yeah.

323
00:22:55,100 --> 00:22:57,033
Why are you so brutal
to the police officers?

324
00:22:58,667 --> 00:23:01,333
800 million pesos worth of shabu
was seized, right?

325
00:23:03,033 --> 00:23:04,933
How many families could be
ruined because of that.

326
00:23:05,067 --> 00:23:06,600
But you don't care, do you?

327
00:23:07,467 --> 00:23:09,067
What? Because you're just
thinking,

328
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:11,367
you want to ruin people who are
already gambling their lives?

329
00:23:12,300 --> 00:23:14,900
That's why you're just
a vlogger.

330
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:17,333
You're just being superficial.

331
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:20,567
News has layers.

332
00:23:21,167 --> 00:23:22,333
You have to dig deeper.

333
00:23:23,300 --> 00:23:24,867
But, word of advice.

334
00:23:25,333 --> 00:23:28,900
What if you just do
beauty content or lifestyle?

335
00:23:31,367 --> 00:23:34,067
Because you might be successful
with that.

336
00:23:34,700 --> 00:23:36,667
Leave journalism

337
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:38,367
to real journalists.

338
00:23:39,767 --> 00:23:41,267
Okay,

339
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,767
JoeyOnDuty?

340
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:48,500
Let's go?

341
00:23:48,633 --> 00:23:50,167
Yeah, let's go.

342
00:24:00,833 --> 00:24:03,133
Are you sure?
You're not in any pain?

343
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:07,200
You didn't break a bone
or hit your head?

344
00:24:07,333 --> 00:24:08,200
Mother...

345
00:24:08,333 --> 00:24:10,133
I should have brought you
with me earlier.

346
00:24:10,267 --> 00:24:11,733
Mother, I'm fine.

347
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,633
Of course, Father is with me.

348
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:15,733
Of course, Father saved me!

349
00:24:15,867 --> 00:24:17,800
It's a good thing he's
a sharpshooter, right,

350
00:24:17,933 --> 00:24:18,833
Father?

351
00:24:19,433 --> 00:24:23,933
So what if you get unlucky,
suddenly miss, and gets hit?

352
00:24:25,567 --> 00:24:26,633
And you,

353
00:24:27,133 --> 00:24:29,300
why did you gamble
with your daughter's life?

354
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:32,333
I wouldn't shoot
if I wasn't sure.

355
00:24:32,900 --> 00:24:34,233
You don't know that.

356
00:24:34,633 --> 00:24:36,500
A lot could happen, Miguel.

357
00:24:36,967 --> 00:24:39,267
Maybe instead of being
praised for being alive.

358
00:24:39,767 --> 00:24:40,867
They'll give you a standing
ovation

359
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:42,133
with your feet level
on the ground.

360
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:46,933
Maybe if they honor me
when I'm dead, you'd be there.

361
00:24:48,267 --> 00:24:50,733
Are you blaming me for leaving?

362
00:24:50,867 --> 00:24:53,300
-We've been waiting for a while!
-I'm following a lead!

363
00:24:53,433 --> 00:24:55,200
Mother, Father, it's okay.

364
00:24:55,867 --> 00:24:58,333
The important thing
is we're safe now,

365
00:24:58,467 --> 00:25:00,000
and we're together, right?

366
00:25:09,033 --> 00:25:10,167
Let's eat.

367
00:25:16,300 --> 00:25:17,600
Let's eat, Love.

368
00:25:19,533 --> 00:25:20,733
Go ahead and eat.

369
00:25:22,533 --> 00:25:23,533
Mother.

370
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:52,767
What's this?

371
00:25:52,900 --> 00:25:55,467
We're repacking shabu,
not pillows!

372
00:25:56,633 --> 00:25:57,833
Repeat it!

373
00:25:59,900 --> 00:26:01,067
That's a waste of space!

374
00:26:01,200 --> 00:26:02,400
We're going to lose money!

375
00:26:02,533 --> 00:26:05,200
- Yes, Boss. Sorry, Boss.
- Repeat it!

376
00:26:05,333 --> 00:26:06,267
You guys!

377
00:26:06,967 --> 00:26:08,500
Work properly!

378
00:26:08,667 --> 00:26:10,200
- Yes, Boss.
- Yes.

379
00:26:17,300 --> 00:26:18,300
Matias.

380
00:26:27,767 --> 00:26:30,767
Almost one billion pesos
worth of drugs.

381
00:26:31,233 --> 00:26:33,400
This is the second shipment
that went wrong.

382
00:26:34,200 --> 00:26:37,133
I thought we already paid
the policeman at the checkpoint?

383
00:26:37,267 --> 00:26:38,700
Ramon is on the payroll.

384
00:26:38,833 --> 00:26:41,400
The one who's not is that pest
Delgado.

385
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:44,067
Why don't we just have him
killed?

386
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:45,133
Lisa,

387
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:47,300
I'll take care of Delgado.

388
00:26:47,633 --> 00:26:49,100
I've already ordered Parak.

389
00:26:49,633 --> 00:26:52,833
Your job is to find Ramon

390
00:26:53,633 --> 00:26:56,533
because I heard he's gone into
hiding.

391
00:26:57,467 --> 00:26:58,833
We should get ahead of him

392
00:26:59,233 --> 00:27:01,467
before he confesses to his
fellow police officers.

393
00:27:04,667 --> 00:27:06,233
I'm telling you, Andrew Dizon.

394
00:27:06,367 --> 00:27:09,567
Everything you say,
you'll eat everything you say!

395
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:11,800
All your slander of the police!

396
00:27:11,933 --> 00:27:14,967
Their heroism is so obvious,
and you're like that.

397
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:16,333
- You're insulting them!
- Hey Joey!

398
00:27:17,233 --> 00:27:18,167
Who's your enemy?

399
00:27:21,500 --> 00:27:22,033
Father.

400
00:27:22,167 --> 00:27:23,533
I heard you downstairs.

401
00:27:23,667 --> 00:27:25,300
I was wondering
who your enemy is.

402
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:30,867
Because I'm pissed
with that Boss Budol.

403
00:27:31,333 --> 00:27:33,100
He disrespected you.

404
00:27:33,500 --> 00:27:35,500
And he also picked on me.

405
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:38,300
Are you really serious
about your vlogging?

406
00:27:38,600 --> 00:27:39,967
Of course!

407
00:27:40,100 --> 00:27:41,967
Especially with people like him.

408
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:43,433
Do you know Father?

409
00:27:43,567 --> 00:27:45,733
He has three million
subscribers.

410
00:27:45,867 --> 00:27:49,700
That means that's how much
he fools with his fake news.

411
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:54,467
So, there should be someone who
shows the heroism of the police.

412
00:27:54,900 --> 00:27:56,000
And that's me.

413
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:00,167
And...

414
00:28:02,733 --> 00:28:03,867
Well, you see.

415
00:28:05,533 --> 00:28:07,133
You and Mother are always
fighting

416
00:28:07,267 --> 00:28:09,133
because you don't have time
for our family anymore

417
00:28:09,267 --> 00:28:11,033
because of your work.

418
00:28:13,667 --> 00:28:14,733
Sorry.

419
00:28:16,367 --> 00:28:17,133
What's that for?

420
00:28:19,700 --> 00:28:22,000
Sorry about what you said...

421
00:28:22,167 --> 00:28:25,600
about my shortcomings to you
and your Mother.

422
00:28:27,600 --> 00:28:29,133
Because I don't have time
for you anymore.

423
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:35,200
And you seldom visit here,
and that's what you see.

424
00:28:38,300 --> 00:28:39,033
Father...

425
00:28:39,833 --> 00:28:40,800
With Mother,

426
00:28:40,933 --> 00:28:42,467
all you have to do is show
a little sweetness.

427
00:28:43,667 --> 00:28:46,300
As for me, you don't need
to worry or do anything

428
00:28:46,433 --> 00:28:49,300
because I understand
your job anyway.

429
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:53,500
Thank you.

430
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:56,500
But you know,

431
00:28:56,633 --> 00:29:01,000
it's not important to me what
good I've done in this world.

432
00:29:02,233 --> 00:29:07,933
What's more important to me
is you and your mother,

433
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:10,167
and your trust in me.

434
00:29:12,767 --> 00:29:14,000
Of course, Father.

435
00:29:15,767 --> 00:29:19,100
By the way,
I have a gift for you.

436
00:29:20,133 --> 00:29:20,833
They say this is trendy now.

437
00:29:20,967 --> 00:29:22,200
This is what is hung on
your bag.

438
00:29:22,333 --> 00:29:25,033
- Ornaments.
- How cute!

439
00:29:25,167 --> 00:29:27,867
I think I just saw
this version today.

440
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,167
Is this fake? Is this original?

441
00:29:29,333 --> 00:29:30,767
This is the first time
I've seen something like this.

442
00:29:30,900 --> 00:29:31,767
I don't know...

443
00:29:31,900 --> 00:29:33,667
someone sold that at the
precinct.

444
00:29:33,800 --> 00:29:34,567
I found it cute.

445
00:29:34,700 --> 00:29:36,100
It's even wearing
a police uniform.

446
00:29:36,233 --> 00:29:38,667
Cute, right?

447
00:29:38,800 --> 00:29:40,333
You'll always keep this?

448
00:29:40,467 --> 00:29:41,700
Hang it in your bag.

449
00:29:42,133 --> 00:29:45,500
So even if I'm not by your side
and you have this with you,

450
00:29:46,033 --> 00:29:47,800
it feels like we're still
together.

451
00:29:48,233 --> 00:29:49,433
Yes, right?

452
00:29:50,133 --> 00:29:51,333
Smile, please.

453
00:29:53,067 --> 00:29:54,533
With teeth.

454
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:55,400
There.

455
00:29:56,367 --> 00:29:58,267
- Right? Cute, right?
- Thank you, Father.

456
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:04,467
<i> You'll always update me.</i>

457
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,100
Don't be like your stubborn
father.

458
00:30:07,233 --> 00:30:09,300
And by the way, go to bed early.

459
00:30:09,433 --> 00:30:13,200
<i>And always remember to eat
a lot for breakfast.</i>

460
00:30:13,333 --> 00:30:16,067
Because that's the most
important meal of the day.

461
00:30:16,733 --> 00:30:20,100
Oh my Mother, why don't you just
record your instructions to me

462
00:30:20,233 --> 00:30:22,900
so you don't get tired
of reminding me?

463
00:30:23,033 --> 00:30:26,767
My child, I'll never get tired.

464
00:30:27,967 --> 00:30:30,433
You know, Mother,
don't worry about me.

465
00:30:30,567 --> 00:30:33,267
I sent you my location.

466
00:30:33,400 --> 00:30:35,900
Also, don't worry about me here
in Manila

467
00:30:36,067 --> 00:30:39,067
because Godfather Diego visits
me from time to time.

468
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:41,500
<i>That's why I'm safe here.
Don't worry.</i>

469
00:30:41,633 --> 00:30:44,667
Mother, it looks like it's going
to rain again.

470
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:47,067
Okay, I'll hurry home.

471
00:30:47,200 --> 00:30:48,133
Love you, Mother.

472
00:30:48,667 --> 00:30:49,967
See you.

473
00:30:50,100 --> 00:30:52,800
Okay. Bye. Love you.

474
00:31:05,467 --> 00:31:08,767
This isn't a residential area
where Ramon's car is parked.

475
00:31:09,633 --> 00:31:11,133
It's impossible for him
to leave it there.

476
00:31:11,800 --> 00:31:14,067
His cellphone can't be reached,
Major.

477
00:31:14,200 --> 00:31:17,800
His wife said his GPS
was last tracked in Sikatuna.

478
00:31:17,933 --> 00:31:21,433
That's 25 kilometers away
from where his car was found.

479
00:31:23,133 --> 00:31:24,567
It looks like he's hiding.

480
00:31:36,933 --> 00:31:38,533
You're going to run away?

481
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:14,800
I won't run away!

482
00:32:28,933 --> 00:32:31,333
And you're still planning
to hide from us.

483
00:32:31,467 --> 00:32:35,133
No, Madam, no!
I really came here to see Parak.

484
00:32:35,267 --> 00:32:36,067
Really?

485
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:37,000
Yes, Madam.

486
00:32:37,133 --> 00:32:39,333
Believe me, Madam.
I won't run away.

487
00:32:49,667 --> 00:32:51,267
Lloyd, check what that is.

488
00:33:03,567 --> 00:33:04,867
Who's that?

489
00:33:05,000 --> 00:33:06,400
Is there someone there?

490
00:33:19,600 --> 00:33:22,067
You really have to do something
about that Miguel Delgado.

491
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:24,767
We've already lost twice
because of that cop.

492
00:33:24,933 --> 00:33:26,367
What do you want to happen,
Boss?

493
00:33:26,500 --> 00:33:27,633
In chess,

494
00:33:27,767 --> 00:33:29,900
what do you do with a piece that
is an obstacle to your plan?

495
00:33:30,033 --> 00:33:30,867
You knock it down.

496
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:32,333
Miguel is a problem.

497
00:33:32,467 --> 00:33:33,833
He's a block in our system.

498
00:33:33,967 --> 00:33:38,000
Andrew, what are you
investigating again?

499
00:33:38,133 --> 00:33:41,033
If you're not up against
high government officials,

500
00:33:41,167 --> 00:33:42,333
it's the police.

501
00:33:42,467 --> 00:33:45,033
Every corner can be caught on
camera,

502
00:33:45,167 --> 00:33:48,567
and they can use that
to identify you, Joey.
